UNDERSTANDING THE QUOTE API
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The planned API integration needs to handle:

• API Endpoint
  - Location from which quote data is requested

• Response Format
  - Application needs quote text and author

• Error Handling
  - Failed requests must be handled

• Loading State
  - User should receive feedback while request is running

• API Limits
  - Any limits imposed by the selected API must be respected

• Browser Access
  - API must permit the relevant browser request scenario


EXPECTED QUOTE FORMAT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "content":
    "The only way to do great work is to love what you do.",

  "author":
    "Steve Jobs"
}


APPLICATION FORMAT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The application uses:

{
  text: '...',
  author: '...'
}


Therefore the API utility transforms:

data.content
    ↓
text


data.author
    ↓
author


================================================================================
INITIAL quoteApi.js SETUP
================================================================================

File:

src/utils/quoteApi.js


// API endpoint for random quotes

const QUOTE_API_URL =
  'https://api.quotable.io/random'


// Fetch a random quote

export const fetchRandomQuote = async () => {

  try {

    // Make API request

    const response =
      await fetch(QUOTE_API_URL)


    // Validate HTTP response

    if (!response.ok) {

      throw new Error(
        `API Error: ${response.status}`
      )
    }


    // Parse response body

    const data =
      await response.json()


    // Convert API shape to application shape

    return {
      text: data.content,
      author: data.author
    }

  } catch (error) {

    console.error(
      'Failed to fetch quote:',
      error
    )


    // Allow caller to handle error

    throw error
  }
}


API UTILITY EXPLANATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------+
| CODE / CONCEPT                       | WHAT IT DOES                          |
+--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------+
| QUOTE_API_URL                        | Stores API endpoint                   |
| fetchRandomQuote                     | Async API utility function            |
| await fetch(...)                     | Performs HTTP request                 |
| response.ok                          | Checks HTTP success status            |
| throw new Error(...)                 | Creates failure path                  |
| response.json()                      | Parses JSON body                      |
| data.content                         | Obtains quote content                 |
| data.author                          | Obtains author                        |
| return {...}                         | Returns app-friendly quote object     |
| catch(error)                         | Handles request/parsing errors        |
| console.error(...)                   | Logs error for debugging              |
| throw error                          | Lets App handle/display the failure   |
+--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------+


